<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qatada ibn Idris</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1220</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qatada ibn Idris was a Hasanid sharif from Yanbu who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in 1201 and founded the line of the Banu Qatada. His descendants ruled Mecca as sharifs under the successive powers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> until 1925, when the Hashemite kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a>.</p></div>
